# Build-time public config for the production frontend (Cloudflare Pages / OpenNext).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* are inlined into the browser bundle by `next build`, so they must exist at
# BUILD time. Cloudflare dashboard "Secrets" are runtime-only and never reach `next build`,
# which is why the app fell back to its in-code localhost default and register hit
# http://127.0.0.1:8000. Every value here is public (it ships to the browser), so it belongs
# in the repo. Do NOT put real secrets (API secret keys, passwords) in any NEXT_PUBLIC_* var.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.personalizemeprints.com

# The SSA forecast service. It IS deployed - Railway, and the live dashboard
# reaches it - but the value is set in the Cloudflare Pages BUILD environment
# rather than here, so this file does not show you what production uses. Check
# the Pages project, not this file. (The comment here used to say the service was
# not deployed at all, which was false and sent a live-outage investigation down
# the wrong path.)
#
# It must be a BUILD variable, not a runtime secret. NEXT_PUBLIC_* are inlined by
# `next build`; with the variable missing at build time the in-code default of
# http://localhost:8001 is baked into the bundle and Demand Forecast, Home and
# Reports all call the VIEWER'S OWN MACHINE. The CSP connect-src in
# next.config.js is built from the same variable, so it would whitelist the wrong
# host too - setting it at runtime only is not enough.
#
# The service also needs SSA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS set to the dashboard origins, or the
# browser blocks the call. Verified against the live host: the preflight returns
# the right allow-origin for personalizemeprints.com, www., and localhost:3000.
#
# The service reads its "now" from BUSINESS_TZ, which defaults to Asia/Manila, so
# it is right on a UTC host without any host configuration. Override it with
# SSA_BUSINESS_TZ only if the shop itself moves - not to match the server. Before
# this it read the host clock, and on any UTC host that put "last complete month"
# a month back and the weekly forecast start a week back, for the eight hours a
# day the UTC date lags Manila's.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SSA_API_URL=https://<the-ssa-host>
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYMONGO_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_ANEE81xYWAFneV3nySjC39mn
